{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And we were, etc., and so we were in their eyes.</b> By this they made known that even the other men who were habituated there did not resemble them, and the proof is that they marveled at them, that they were as grasshoppers by reason of the extraordinary smallness of their bodies — from this you learn that those who were habituated with them were not of this likeness."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:38.208923964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}